# Data Dictionary – Retail Sales Dataset

This document describes the structure and meaning of each column in the
Retail Sales dataset used for SQL business reporting and KPI analysis.



# Table: RetailSales

| Column Name     | Data Type        | Description |
|-----------------|------------------|-------------|
| OrderID         | VARCHAR          | Unique identifier for each customer order |
| OrderDate       | DATE             | Date when the order was placed |
| CustomerID      | VARCHAR          | Unique identifier for each customer |
| CustomerName    | VARCHAR          | Name of the customer |
| Region          | VARCHAR          | Geographic region of the customer |
| ProductID       | VARCHAR          | Unique identifier for the product |
| ProductName     | VARCHAR          | Product name |
| Category        | VARCHAR          | Product category (Electronics / Accessories) |
| Quantity        | INT              | Number of units purchased |
| UnitPrice       | DECIMAL          | Price per unit |
| Revenue         | DECIMAL          | Total sales value (Quantity × UnitPrice) |
| Cost            | DECIMAL          | Total cost associated with the product |
| Margin          | DECIMAL          | Profit (Revenue − Cost) |



# Calculated Fields

- **Revenue** = Quantity × UnitPrice  
- **Margin** = Revenue − Cost  
- **Gross Margin %** = (Margin ÷ Revenue) × 100  

These calculated values were validated through reconciliation checks.



# Data Integrity
- OrderID is assumed to be unique per transaction
- No NULL values exist in critical financial fields
- All numeric values use consistent units
